Subject: [PATCH] test: make managed-injector parametrize robust to external cred types

Under the Automation Platform product identity, load_credentials() registers
the external-secret credential types (HashiCorp Vault, Conjur, CyberArk AIM,
Azure KV, AWS SM, Delinea, GitHub App, ...) into ManagedCredentialType.registry
via CredentialType.load_plugin(), which stores them as
`SimpleNamespace(kind='external', backend=...)` with NO `injectors` attribute
(external creds inject through a backend lookup, not static injectors — this is
upstream's own design at credential.py:load_plugin).

Upstream's test at test_tasks.py:1639 builds its parametrize list with a bare
`if cls.injectors`, which assumes every registry entry has an `injectors`
attribute — true only under the plain-AWX identity where the external types are
gated off. With patch 0007 those types are (correctly) present, so the bare
attribute access raises AttributeError at COLLECTION time and aborts the entire
module. Runtime is unaffected: production code branches on `kind == 'external'`
(CredentialTypeHelper.get_creation_params) and never reads `.injectors` on these.

Fix: use `getattr(cls, 'injectors', None)`. This preserves the test's intent
(parametrize over managed types that HAVE injectors) while correctly excluding
the external, injector-less types instead of crashing on them. Test-only change.

diff --git a/awx/main/tests/unit/test_tasks.py b/awx/main/tests/unit/test_tasks.py
index 68b4d8e..599d34c 100644
--- a/awx/main/tests/unit/test_tasks.py
+++ b/awx/main/tests/unit/test_tasks.py
@@ -1636,7 +1636,7 @@ def test_acquire_lock_acquisition_fail_logged(fcntl_lockf, logger_mock, os_close
     )
 
 
-@pytest.mark.parametrize('injector_cls', [cls for cls in ManagedCredentialType.registry.values() if cls.injectors])
+@pytest.mark.parametrize('injector_cls', [cls for cls in ManagedCredentialType.registry.values() if getattr(cls, 'injectors', None)])
 def test_managed_injector_redaction(injector_cls):
     """See awx.main.models.inventory.PluginFileInjector._get_shared_env
